+   "source": [
+    "# TERRA tutorial - spatial mapping of perturbation effects (test section)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Compute a **per-cell** perturbation score with `infer_token_distance` (W2 between each cell's unperturbed and perturbed token-embedding clouds) and **project it back onto the tissue** to see *where* the glomerular knockout has its effect.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "> **Requirements:** a GPU, and `terra-st` installed with the perturbation extra:\n",
+    "> `pip install \"terra-st[perturb]\" gdown`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This tutorial runs **end-to-end on a de-identified test kidney section we provide** using the public [`lotfollahi-lab/TERRA-96M`](https://huggingface.co/lotfollahi-lab/TERRA-96M) model. Expensive steps (tokenisation, perturbation) are **cached** locally — the first run computes them, later runs (and the other tutorials) reuse the cache."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ef3fa5ce",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 1. Setup"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "1ea4a45b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# !pip install -q \"terra-st[perturb]\" gdown   # uncomment on first run"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "9e4b03d6",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import os\n",
+    "from pathlib import Path\n",
+    "\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "import pandas as pd\n",
+    "import scanpy as sc\n",
+    "import anndata as ad\n",
+    "import torch\n",
+    "from datasets import load_from_disk\n",
+    "\n",
+    "from terra import download_pretrained\n",
+    "from terra.inference import harmonize_adata, tokenize_adata\n",
+    "from terra.inference import perturb_dataset, infer_token_distance\n",
+    "import squidpy as sq\n",
+    "\n",
+    "sc.settings.set_figure_params(dpi=80, frameon=False)\n",
+    "import logging; logging.basicConfig(level=\"INFO\")  # show TERRA progress"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "af4e0f35",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 2. Configuration\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Set the model, the section data file, and a local cache directory. If you host the test-section `.h5ad` on Google Drive, put its file id in `DRIVE_FILE_ID` and it will be downloaded automatically."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "3febaccc",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "MODEL_REPO   = \"lotfollahi-lab/TERRA-96M\"   # HF model bundle\n",
+    "SECTION      = \"K014\"\n",
+    "NICHE_KEY    = \"NEMO_updated_niche\"           # obs column used to group / colour\n",
+    "DEVICE       = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
+    "\n",
+    "DATA_H5AD    = \"K014_full.h5ad\"          # local path to the section AnnData\n",
+    "DRIVE_FILE_ID = \"11C6z0RZXZhbKzI8SHSRbsA_k1i1Tqsfa\"  # optional: gdown fallback\n",
+    "\n",
+    "CACHE        = Path(\"cache\"); CACHE.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
+    "TOK_CACHE    = CACHE / f\"{SECTION}_tokenized\"          # shared across tutorials\n",
+    "print(\"device:\", DEVICE)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "5df3c12f",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 3. Download the pretrained model (Hugging Face)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "`download_pretrained` fetches the model bundle (`model_checkpoint.pt`, `model_config.yaml`, `token_dictionary.pkl`) and returns its local path."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "3d083a6b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "model_dir = download_pretrained(MODEL_REPO)\n",
+    "print(\"model bundle:\", model_dir)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "c992aa68",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 4. Load the section data\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The provided test-section `.h5ad` holds raw counts (`X`), spatial coordinates (`obsm['spatial']`) and niche / cell-type labels for the whole test section (123,563 cells)."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "5bdc5f6b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "if not os.path.exists(DATA_H5AD):\n",
+    "    import gdown\n",
+    "    print(\"downloading section data from Google Drive ...\")\n",
+    "    gdown.download(id=DRIVE_FILE_ID, output=DATA_H5AD, quiet=False)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "adata = sc.read_h5ad(DATA_H5AD)\n",
+    "if \"cell_id\" not in adata.obs.columns:\n",
+    "    adata.obs[\"cell_id\"] = adata.obs_names.astype(str)\n",
+    "adata.obs[\"cell_id\"] = adata.obs[\"cell_id\"].astype(str)\n",
+    "print(adata)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "5350527a",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 5. Harmonise & tokenise (cached)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "`harmonize_adata` maps gene symbols to the model's Ensembl vocabulary and filters low-quality cells/genes. `tokenize_adata` turns the neighbourhood into the gene-token sequences the model consumes. **This is the slow step**, so the result is cached — delete `cache/` to recompute, or drop in a pre-computed tokenised dataset to skip it."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "ac50c47e",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "adata = harmonize_adata(adata)\n",
+    "print(f\"after harmonise: {adata.n_obs:,} cells x {adata.n_vars:,} genes\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "if TOK_CACHE.exists():\n",
+    "    print(\"loading cached tokenised dataset ...\")\n",
+    "    tok = load_from_disk(str(TOK_CACHE))\n",
+    "else:\n",
+    "    print(\"tokenising (first run; will be cached) ...\")\n",
+    "    tok = tokenize_adata(adata, model_dir, str(CACHE / \"tok_tmp\"), nproc=4)\n",
+    "    tok.save_to_disk(str(TOK_CACHE))\n",
+    "tok.set_format(\"torch\", columns=[\"rel_x_coord\", \"rel_y_coord\", \"cell_id\",\n",
+    "                                 \"gene_tokens\", \"gene_expr\", \"n_nonzero_tokens\"])\n",
+    "print(f\"tokenised cells: {len(tok):,}\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "08d16ae1",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 6. Perturb (cached)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Glomerular filtration-barrier knockout (NPNT/WT1/MAGI1) in cell + neighbourhood, all cells; `return_only_perturbed_cells=True` keeps the affected subset. Reuses the shared cache if present."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "c9ba4deb",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "genes = [\"ENSG00000168743\", \"ENSG00000184937\", \"ENSG00000151276\"]  # NPNT, WT1, MAGI1\n",
+    "perturb_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
